{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CesXdCWeEtTBNvNYPfwhC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Repository findings:**\n- Shipment model: `src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:9`\n- ShipmentController: `src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt:20`\n- ShipmentRepository: `src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt:10`\n- Error handling: `src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiExceptions.kt:11`\n- Error codes: `src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt:31`\n\n**Conventions:**\n1. Controllers use `@RestController` with `@RequestMapping(\"/shipments\")`\n2. Error handling throws exceptions: `ResourceNotFoundException` (404), `ConflictException` (409)\n3. Error codes are defined in a closed enum in `ApiError.kt`\n4. Repository pattern with in-memory store and `save()` method\n5. Tests use `@SpringBootTest`, `@AutoConfigureMockMvc`, and `MockMvc` with request builders\n6. All existing tests pass (13 tests, 0 failures)\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ShipmentController.kt` - Add `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` endpoint\n2. `ApiError.kt` - Add error code for invalid shipment state transitions\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` - Add tests for the confirm endpoint\n\n**Risks:**\n1. Breaking existing tests if endpoint doesn't integrate properly\n2. Incorrectly handling state transitions (must allow CREATED→CONFIRMED and retry on already-CONFIRMED)\n3. Not handling CANCELLED state correctly (409 required)\n\n**Open questions:** None; the ticket clearly defines all four cases (CREATED, already CONFIRMED, CANCELLED, not found).\n\nNow I'll move to DESIGN.\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** - Add error code `INVALID_SHIPMENT_STATE` to the `ErrorCode` enum to handle state transition conflicts\n   \n2. **ShipmentController.kt** - Add a new `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` method that:\n   - Retrieves the shipment by ID (throw `ResourceNotFoundException` if not found)\n   - Checks the current status:\n     - If `CREATED`: transition to `CONFIRMED`\n     - If already `CONFIRMED`: do nothing (allow retry)\n     - If `CANCELLED`: throw `ConflictException` with the new error code\n   - Save the (possibly updated) shipment and return it with HTTP 200\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Add tests for each case:\n   - Confirming a CREATED shipment moves it to CONFIRMED and returns 200\n   - Confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds (idempotent)\n   - Confirming a CANCELLED shipment returns 409 with error code\n   - Confirming a non-existent shipment returns 404 with error code\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Creating a separate service layer for state transitions: Rejected because the existing codebase doesn't have a service layer; controllers directly manipulate repositories. Following convention is better than introducing new patterns.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Input | Processing | Output | Status |\n|------|-------|-----------|--------|--------|\n| Confirm CREATED | shipmentId (path param) | Retrieve shipment, check status is CREATED, update to CONFIRMED, save | Shipment JSON | 200 |\n| Confirm already CONFIRMED | shipmentId (path param) | Retrieve shipment, check status is CONFIRMED, do nothing, return current | Shipment JSON | 200 |\n| Confirm CANCELLED | shipmentId (path param) | Retrieve shipment, check status is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException | Error envelope with INVALID_SHIPMENT_STATE code | 409 |\n| Unknown shipment | shipmentId (path param) | Retrieve returns null, throw ResourceNotFoundException | Error envelope with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code | 404 |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n1. `confirms a created shipment to confirmed status` - POST confirm on CREATED, expect 200 with status=CONFIRMED\n2. `confirms an already confirmed shipment succeeds` - Create and confirm twice, second should succeed with 200 and no changes\n3. `rejects confirming a cancelled shipment with conflict` - Directly insert CANCELLED shipment in repo, POST confirm, expect 409 with INVALID_SHIPMENT_STATE code\n4. `reports unknown shipment when confirming` - POST confirm on non-existent ID, expect 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nLet me now implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3414,"cache_read_input_tokens":14886,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3414},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5f263cc5-3a8c-4856-9606-c45855fb4707","uuid":"9b7dbba1-b2d4-4756-bed6-22b2e693b080","timestamp":"2026-09-09T08:12:32.235Z","request_id":"req_011CesXdBtRiBJJB78bgAdyE"}
